Z||000017||JimiZ||08-28-99||12:05 AM||||I gotta put my 2 cents in for this'n.  <br>I love all cars ('cept Yugos), for being what they are.  My first car was a VW Beetle.  I got it when I was 15, and me and my dad spent a lot of quality time together fixing it up. I wanted it to have the "Cal" look.  We took off all the chrome, removed the blinkers from the fenders, re-did the seats, added a console, put in a stereo, put 235/60/15 tires on the back, turned the torsion bars and jacked it up, added a 930 porsche whale tail to it, and painted it yellow.  It was the coolest car.  It was ready on my 16th birthday.  It was slow.  It was under-designed, but I loved and will always love that car.  Just thinking about it makes me teary eyed (let's hug).  But, even then, there were other kids with Bugs, who I didn't like.  They gave them a bad name.  Little Punks out driving.  I think that's probably what you hate about v-dubs with the cantelope shooters on the back.  I myself think they look cool, but too many lil punks drive them.<br>OK, there's my 2 cents worth.  Thanks for reading.  On to better things....Like a 4.3L Fiero conversion....yeh....heh...heh....
